<%# One question: does this reel play, at a point a real break would actually start from?
    Deliberately bare -- no channel, no schedule, nothing that could fail and be mistaken
    for the reel failing. The same shape as sources#test, for the same reason. %>
<div class="reel-preview"
     data-controller="reel-preview"
     data-reel-preview-frame-value="reelPreviewFrame">
  <div class="reel-preview__bar">
    <strong><%= @reel.label %></strong>
    <code><%= @reel.youtube_id %></code>

    <span class="reel-preview__meta">
      covers <%= reel_years(@reel) %>
    </span>

    <%# The whole point of the page: what the schedule would have picked, spelled out, so a
        reel that plays and a reel that happens to have been given an easy offset are not
        the same result. %>
    <span class="reel-preview__meta">
      starting <%= clock(@offset) %> in<% if @reel.duration_seconds.to_i.positive? %>
        of <%= reel_length(@reel) %><% end %>
    </span>

    <span class="reel-preview__meta">
      for a <%= clock(@break_seconds) %> break
    </span>

    <%= link_to 'Roll again', preview_admin_commercial_reel_path(@reel), class: 'reel-preview__link' %>
    <%= link_to 'Back to the reels', admin_commercial_reels_path, class: 'reel-preview__link' %>
  </div>

  <% if @embed_url %>
    <p class="reel-preview__note">
      This is the embed a break uses, at an offset rolled the way a break rolls one — never
      the first <%= CommercialReel::INTRO_SKIP %> seconds, where the compilation's own titles
      sit, and never so late that a <%= clock(@break_seconds) %> break would run off the end.
      <%= link_to 'Open it on YouTube', "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=#{@reel.youtube_id}&t=#{@offset}",
                  target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener noreferrer' %>
      to rule out anything on this page.
    </p>

    <%# Hidden until the player says it will not play. On /cable this is a caption over the
        break; here it is the answer the page exists to give, so it says what went wrong. %>
    <div class="reel-preview__failure" data-reel-preview-target="failure" hidden>
      <h2>YouTube will not play this reel</h2>
      <p data-reel-preview-target="reason">The player refused it.</p>
      <p>
        On /cable this is a black rectangle for the length of the break — the caption covers
        it, but there are no adverts. Swap the id for a compilation that still plays, or
        delete the reel and let the year fall back to its neighbour.
      </p>
    </div>

    <iframe class="reel-preview__frame"
            id="reelPreviewFrame"
            title="<%= @reel.label %> preview"
            allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture"
            src="<%= @embed_url %>"></iframe>
  <% else %>
    <p class="reel-preview__note reel-preview__note--empty">
      There is no active YouTube provider, so no embed address can be built. Add one under
      <%= link_to 'sources', sources_path %> — every reel plays through it, which is why the
      domain lives in one row rather than in each of these.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
